nd.","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":14,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh, who were among those who had spied out the land, tore their clothes","from":6},{"book":"NUM","chapter":34,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"These are their names: Caleb son of Jephunneh from the tribe of Judah;","from":6},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":9,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Moses said to Joshua, “Choose some of our men and go out to fight the Amalekites. Tomorrow I will stand on the hilltop with the staff of God in my hand.” Joshua did as Moses had instructed him and fought against the Amalekites, while Moses, Aaron, and Hur went up to the top of the hill. As long as Moses held up his hands, Israel prevailed; but when he lowered them, Amalek prevailed. When Mosesʼ hands grew heavy, they took a stone and put it under him, and he sat on it. Then Aaron and Hur held his hands up, one on each side, so that his hands remained steady until the sun went down. So Joshua overwhelmed Amalek and his army with the sword.","from":8},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Moses said to Joshua, “Choose some of our men and go out to fight the Amalekites. Tomorrow I will stand on the hilltop with the staff of God in my hand.”","from":16},{"book":"EXO","chapter":18,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Moses chose capable men from all Israel and made them heads over the people as leaders of thousands, of hundreds, of fifties, and of tens.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":11},{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":4}]},"17-24":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"ahiman-h0289g","name":"Ahiman","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse